{"id":"f7e1d3c1baa2af88","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-birkhoff-variety.md","title":"Birkhoff Variety Theorem","display":"Birkhoff Variety Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-birkhoff-variety","aliases":["93-thm-birkhoff-variety"],"display":"Birkhoff Variety Theorem","depends_on":["[[93-df-variety]]","[[93-df-closure-operators]]","[[93-df-similarity-type]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-birkhoff-variety"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-birkhoff-variety</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Birkhoff Variety Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" href=\"?note=f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" title=\"93-df-variety\">93-df-variety</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"97b46a497e251f9f\" href=\"?note=97b46a497e251f9f\" title=\"93-df-closure-operators\">93-df-closure-operators</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" href=\"?note=ee84ed8b0fae5bc3\" title=\"93-df-similarity-type\">93-df-similarity-type</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-birkhoff-variety-—-Birkhoff-Variety-Theorem\">thm-birkhoff-variety — Birkhoff Variety Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\">\\(\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\}\">\\(\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HSP}_{\\tau}\">\\(\\mathrm{HSP}_{\\tau}\\)</span> are sourced from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" href=\"?note=f0b0edbaa6696a1d\" title=\"93-df-variety\">93-df-variety</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"97b46a497e251f9f\" href=\"?note=97b46a497e251f9f\" title=\"93-df-closure-operators\">93-df-closure-operators</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}birkhoff\\text{-}variety}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\\land\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\}\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal K;\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathcal K=\\mathrm{HSP}_{\\tau}(\\mathcal K)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}birkhoff\\text{-}variety}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{SimType}_{93}(\\tau)\\land\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\{\\mathbf A:\\mathrm{Alg}_{\\tau}(\\mathbf A)\\}\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Variety}_{93}(\\mathcal K;\\tau)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathcal K=\\mathrm{HSP}_{\\tau}(\\mathcal K)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Birkhoff's Variety Theorem states that a class of algebras is a variety (equationally defined) if and only if it is closed under homomorphic images, subalgebras, and direct products. This is the fundamental characterization of varieties in universal algebra.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-birkhoff-variety-—-Birkhoff-Variety-Theorem","text":"thm-birkhoff-variety — Birkhoff Variety Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-variety","status":"resolved","id":"f0b0edbaa6696a1d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","e